Z||000007||curtis||10-09-2001||08:36 AM||||We talked to a Fiero mechanic yesterday and told him what happened he said that the o ring seal on the distributor gave out, and because of the oil pressure it threw oil out onto the exhaust. On his he changes that seal quite often.||||reg||4
Z||000008||Denny||10-09-2001||01:19 PM||||Damn! Sorry to hear that!<P>I doubt very much that it was the distributor seal. A more likely suspect is the o-ring seal at the fuel-rail fitting for the cold-start tube. That o-ring breaks down with age and leaks fuel under pressure. I've replaced the rings on three V6's I've owned, and we had to do Gargoyle86's a couple of years ago.<P>The lesson here is if you smell gas at the engine compartment, especially just after shutting the engine off, look for a leak at this fitting. You can see it just past the right side of the distributor cap, at the end of the fuel rail. If it's leaking DO NOT DRIVE THE CAR! It's a fire waiting to happen!<P>An o-ring kit is available for around $8 +shipping from  <A HREF="http://www.gmpartsdirect.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.gmpartsdirect.com</A> , and it's an easy job.<P>I wrote an article about it for the MAFOA newsletter, I'll see if I can get Bob (Gargoyle86) to post it on the Pride website. We'll let you know . . .<P>I'll add the part # here when I get home tonight.||||reg||4
Z||000009||Denny||10-09-2001||04:55 PM||||The O-ring kit part # is 17111954.  <A HREF="http://www.gmpartsdirect.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.gmpartsdirect.com/</A>  lists the kit for $7.68 +shipping.||||reg||1
Z||000010||88CoupeV6||10-09-2001||05:32 PM||||Sorry to hear about that  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I had my distributor o-ring go on me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> The thing just sprays oil. It is a quick, cheap fix. I think the o-ring is like $3.00<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig.jpg">    <BR>:D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||9
Z||000011||Denny||10-09-2001||09:13 PM||||Here's the link to the Technical page at    <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/technical.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieropride.com/technical.htm</A> .<P>Select "Cold Start O-Ring Replacement" (or any other article you want   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">).<p>[This message has been edited by Denny (edited 10-09-2001).]||||reg||10
