Z||000013||artherd||10-10-2001||03:00 AM||||Curtis?  SGI-man?  <P>Please tell me it's you (though you live on Cobb Mountian...)  <P>PLEASE oh please tell me that I do not know *TWO* people named Curtis that have had 88 Formulas burn up on them....<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000014||dennis_6||10-10-2001||03:10 AM||||My 86 Fiero SE blew a hole in the side of the distributor cap.  Shut the car off just in time.  Turned out to be a leaking cold start oring.  This Oring is not on the fuel rail, it sits ontop of the intake manifold.||||reg||1
