Z||000016||Denny||10-10-2001||07:28 AM||||It was not my intent to start an argument here. I suppose I could have said "It's also possible . . ." instead of "I doubt . . ."<P>Anyway, I agree that an oil leak of sufficient volume dumping oil on the headers could also start a fire, especially on the stock headers that haven't been modified to remove the excess metal from the inside. The excess metal blocks the exhaust flow and gets hot enough to cause the headers to glow red at those points. Those and the stock cat are the only parts of the exhaust system that get sufficiently hot enough to ignite oil.<P>So, it <I>is</I> possible. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||7
