Z||000019||htiek||10-12-2001||11:13 AM||||Wow thats no good.<BR>I actually know how it feels, my 84 did something similar.  Although my fire started when i was starting the car. The problem was the computer shorted out and opened the injector to full throttle and the gas overfilled the bowl.<P>One back fire later and my engine was smoking.  I was lucky however i was near a building that had a fire extinguisher, so i ran, got it, put it out, and towed it home.<P>All the damage cost me around 40 to fix, all junk yard parts.  The most expensive parts were the sensors, and those were junked.<P>Damn fire prone fiero's!!!<P><BR>||||reg||1
